      "id": 1,
      "text": "Westlake earned its name in 2015, drawing inspiration from neighboring Weston and its emphasis on artificial lakes and master‑planned design.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Westlake%2C_Florida",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Former farmland known as the Seminole Improvement District became Westlake in 2014 when Minto Communities bought 3,800 acres for $51 million.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Westlake%2C_Florida",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Westlake officially joined Palm Beach County as its 39th municipality on June 22 2016 after a special election.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Westlake%2C_Florida",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The U.S. Postal Service began treating Westlake as a distinct municipality on September 15 2017.",
